The digital number is transmitted and then converted to an analogue form by the digital-to-analogue converter (DAC).

Use data from Fig. 6.2 to draw, on the axes of Fig. 6.3, the output level of the DAC for time $t = 0$ to time $t = 1.50\text{ ms}$. Assume that there is no time delay of the transmission of the signal between point $P$ and the output of the DAC.

